      "text": "The number of days from November 23 to December 23 is 46 days. (Proof: 23 + 30 = 53; 53 / 7= 7 R 4.)\nThe last Thursday of November is November 30.\nNor, since 46 / 7 = 6 R 4, November 23 and December 23 are 4 days apart.\n\nSince Friday is 4 days before Thursday, December 23 occurs on a Monday.\nThe answer is 1. To solve this problem, I need to figure out the day of the week on December 23 given that it falls on the same day as Thanksgiving, considering some of the given details.\n\nStep 1: Identify the given information.\n- Thanksgiving will be on Thursday, November 23.\n- November has 30 days.\n\nStep 2: Calculate the number of days from November 23 to December 23.\n- According to the problem statement, there are 46 days from November 23 to December 23.\n- Since we're dealing only with complete weeks (7 days), we can round this number. \n- 46 days = 47 * 1 = 47 days (integer part)\n- The remainder of 6 cannot be rounded down because we still need to reach December 23.\n- So, the calculation becomes a bit more accurate:\n\nStep 3: Find out what day of the week happens 6 days later than Thursday.\n- Counting 6 days from Thursday:\n  - Thursday + 1 day = Friday\n  - Friday + 1 day = Saturday\n  - Saturday + 1 day = Sunday\n  - Sunday + 1 day = Monday\n  - Monday + 1 day = Tuesday\n- Therefore, December 23 will be on a Monday.\n\nSo, the day of the week on December 23 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
