      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving (on November 23) is a Thursday, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the days between November 23 and December 23:**\n   - Since we know that November 23 is a Thursday, we need to count the number of days until December 23 while noting the day of the week for each date.\n\n2. **Count the days from November 23 to November 30:**\n   - November has 30 days in its middle section after the beginning.\n   - Days in November after November 23:\n     - 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30\n   - Total days spent from November 23 to November 30: \\( 7 \\) days (inclusive).\n\n3. **Determine the day of the week for November 30:**\n   - Since November 23 is a Thursday, seven days later take us to July (since 7 mod 7 = 0, so we wrap around to the beginning of the month).\n   - Thus, November 30 is also a Thursday.\n\n4. **Count the days from November 30 to December 23:**\n   - November 30 is a Thursday.\n\n5. **Add the days to October 1 follows directly to December 23:**\n   - Working backwards from the December 23, pointed from November 30 is four more days before it reaches November 30.\n\n6. **Calculate the new day of the week:**\n   - We start at a Thursday and add each additional day to determine what day it will fall on next:\n     - 1 day = Friday\n     - 2 days = Saturday\n     - 3 days = Sunday\n     - 4 days = Monday\n\nTherefore, December 23, given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday (November 23), falls on **Monday**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Monday}}\n\\]",
